                        ],
                        "form": "den Anbruch"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8b5c92f2-608c-439b-8728-9cc678945747",
                        "entry_id": "cb5743fa-81a7-31c5-97f9-22f1518376e1",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Anbrüche"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6a8fcb6e-23ba-3a93-a1dc-0f8793b25c04",
                        "entry_id": "cb5743fa-81a7-31c5-97f9-22f1518376e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "zeitliche Definition im Sinne von Beginn, zum Beispiel einer Tageszeit oder eines Zeitalters"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f23f240e-8236-4ac3-a150-0c77f99750f0",
                                "sense_id": "6a8fcb6e-23ba-3a93-a1dc-0f8793b25c04",
                                "text": "Der Sonnenaufgang kennzeichnet den Anbruch eines neuen Tages."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6fdc0f41-9506-41ca-a9b8-c071ebed50e0",
                                "sense_id": "6a8fcb6e-23ba-3a93-a1dc-0f8793b25c04",
                                "text": "„Zwei Jahrhunderte lang, seit Anbruch des Industriezeitalters, wurde das Revier durchbuddelt und durchfurcht.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1bb35af4-cf8f-46de-bce6-9c56294004bf",
                                "sense_id": "6a8fcb6e-23ba-3a93-a1dc-0f8793b25c04",
                                "text": "„Mit Anbruch des folgenden Tages holte Han Dau-go die Ladenschlüssel aus Simen Tjing's Wohnanwesen, öffnete das Geschäft und schenkte der alten Feng zum Dank eine Unze Silber.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a8f0c38-fafa-3b91-9a78-2c2d93e186d3",
                        "entry_id": "cb5743fa-81a7-31c5-97f9-22f1518376e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "erstmaliges Öffnen eines befüllten und verschlossenen Behältnisses"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Lebensmittel"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "063ef7fc-2c35-4fe0-9c79-220f01bcbd07",
                                "sense_id": "7a8f0c38-fafa-3b91-9a78-2c2d93e186d3",
                                "text": "Nach Anbruch sollte das Produkt innerhalb weniger Tage verzehrt werden."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52366609-1cba-4e7a-bf2c-d9f28b2f40bb",
                                "sense_id": "7a8f0c38-fafa-3b91-9a78-2c2d93e186d3",
                                "text": "„[Augentropfen] sollten handwarm sein und nach Anbruch der Packung innerhalb von 6 Wochen verbraucht werden.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4138ac32-a801-30cc-a79c-566affb69eb4",
                        "entry_id": "cb5743fa-81a7-31c5-97f9-22f1518376e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "im Bergbau übliche Bezeichnung der Stelle, an der eine Lagerstätte angetroffen wird, speziell auch einen bloßgelegten Erzgang"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Bergmannssprache"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4df11724-e09e-49b0-9a12-fef039a08fb1",
                                "sense_id": "4138ac32-a801-30cc-a79c-566affb69eb4",
                                "text": "Der Anbruch wurde vom Vorarbeiter farblich markiert."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2745065e-c270-455d-89a1-44a0a153f5a4",
                                "sense_id": "4138ac32-a801-30cc-a79c-566affb69eb4",
                                "text": "„Nach der physikalisch-ökunomischen Wochenschrift lautete die Denkschrift: ‚Auf dem St. Christophs-Erbstollen, Fundgrubner- und St. Wolfgangsstollen sind Pucherze am Anbruch gehauen werden, werden aber dermalen nicht betrieben. […]‘“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "48ea700d-4769-3698-89e2-a2ea3f58c299",
                        "entry_id": "cb5743fa-81a7-31c5-97f9-22f1518376e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "morsch gewordenes und nicht mehr beilfestes Holz, angefaultes Holz"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Forstwesen"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b4ff1dd-9e95-4398-a0c0-0e50e682dfd7",
                                "sense_id": "48ea700d-4769-3698-89e2-a2ea3f58c299",
                                "text": "Am Wegesrand liegen mehrere Haufen mit Anbrüchen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"4\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ddb38a9b-0939-3d42-bed3-cbe3e7cdde99",
                        "entry_id": "cb5743fa-81a7-31c5-97f9-22f1518376e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "beschädigte Stelle, die zur Zerstörung führen kann"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "af1cd41a-ceba-4676-9f59-3ec56c4f2b09",
                                "sense_id": "ddb38a9b-0939-3d42-bed3-cbe3e7cdde99",
                                "text": "Ich kann noch keine Anbrüche erkennen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"5\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "591adc1a-40e2-468b-b2cd-125d88a356c0",
                        "source_entry_id": "cb5743fa-81a7-31c5-97f9-22f1518376e1",
                        "source_sense_id": "6a8fcb6e-23ba-3a93-a1dc-0f8793b25c04",
                        "source_sense_description": "zeitliche Definition im Sinne von Beginn",
                        "target_lang_word": "dawn",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dawn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "433cf67d-0cce-39d8-a270-44c93df8b157",
                                        "entry_id": "4f000209-4f6c-33bf-bab6-c115875f06ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To begin to brighten with daylight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "525d770d-2d40-4a07-a5e5-13b80b09343c",
                                                "sense_id": "433cf67d-0cce-39d8-a270-44c93df8b157",
                                                "text": "A new day dawns."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a80618f7-3053-47ad-8330-541627db54e9",
                                                "sense_id": "433cf67d-0cce-39d8-a270-44c93df8b157",
                                                "text": "In the end of the Sabbath, as it began to dawn toward the first day of the week, came Mary Magdalene[…]to see the sepulchre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c960e470-27d4-3029-ae37-1c6f2c3ada35",
                                        "entry_id": "4f000209-4f6c-33bf-bab6-c115875f06ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To start to appear or become obvious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0860a732-8707-4483-977c-6f7825cf8c14",
                                                "sense_id": "c960e470-27d4-3029-ae37-1c6f2c3ada35",
                                                "text": "I don’t want to be there when the truth dawns on him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b5aff9b-74a5-4192-a5a8-739eb220d107",
                                                "sense_id": "c960e470-27d4-3029-ae37-1c6f2c3ada35",
                                                "text": "The realization dawned on him that few would pass that final exam."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "774fb426-830c-4224-9310-e6fce5fe08bb",
                                                "sense_id": "c960e470-27d4-3029-ae37-1c6f2c3ada35",
                                                "text": "Although the Celebrity was almost impervious to sarcasm, he was now beginning to exhibit visible signs of uneasiness, the consciousness dawning upon him that his eccentricity was not receiving the ovation it merited."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eaed0127-42c6-3dc2-88df-f3d168a2debc",
                                        "entry_id": "4f000209-4f6c-33bf-bab6-c115875f06ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To begin to give promise; to begin to appear or to expand."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fe80185-bbe8-4597-82bb-2d7bf230019e",
                                                "sense_id": "eaed0127-42c6-3dc2-88df-f3d168a2debc",
                                                "text": "when life awakes, and dawns at every line"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c68712d-a5d2-4a82-8b93-dfabaf52c2d6",
                                                "sense_id": "eaed0127-42c6-3dc2-88df-f3d168a2debc",
                                                "text": "in dawning youth"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e9199f4-90e8-4364-9b1d-3c3abdcc5727",
                                                "sense_id": "eaed0127-42c6-3dc2-88df-f3d168a2debc",
                                                "text": "Leave the time of war behind and let a time of peace dawn!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dawn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8151050-695b-344c-bddd-cd3a3de83bd1",
                                        "entry_id": "34bced4c-7f31-378e-9c5f-92de88306027",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25a1c109-0f40-3139-8363-11ee4128788c",
                                        "entry_id": "34bced4c-7f31-378e-9c5f-92de88306027",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The rising of the sun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bfb66ef-5f02-4086-8d3c-d62c7644c509",
                                                "sense_id": "25a1c109-0f40-3139-8363-11ee4128788c",
                                                "text": "Every act of a Roman, from birth to death, from dawn to night, was controlled and supervised by some presiding deity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9496646f-514e-3b87-b5cc-378971fa4b63",
                                        "entry_id": "34bced4c-7f31-378e-9c5f-92de88306027",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The time when the sun rises."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9f782f3-1372-4ec5-b9f3-7a09e9717c12",
                                                "sense_id": "9496646f-514e-3b87-b5cc-378971fa4b63",
                                                "text": "She rose before dawn to meet the train."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c492c4a9-1f2c-3f2f-9a8f-619e990b2214",
                                        "entry_id": "34bced4c-7f31-378e-9c5f-92de88306027",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The earliest phase of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ffb8908-53ca-4990-9a4a-d9609da2dea6",
                                                "sense_id": "c492c4a9-1f2c-3f2f-9a8f-619e990b2214",
                                                "text": "The dawn of civilization didn't imply twilight of barbarity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e33f9d4-9f4a-4562-acde-b0dcdd7c3cbc",
                                                "sense_id": "c492c4a9-1f2c-3f2f-9a8f-619e990b2214",
                                                "text": "The dawn of the oil age was fairly recent. Although the stuff was used to waterproof boats in the Middle East 6,000 years ago, extracting it in earnest began only in 1859 after an oil strike in Pennsylvania. The first barrels of crude fetched $18 (around $450 at today’s prices)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a9196306-f537-487a-931e-41d5a2d3e5a6",
                        "source_entry_id": "cb5743fa-81a7-31c5-97f9-22f1518376e1",
                        "source_sense_id": "6a8fcb6e-23ba-3a93-a1dc-0f8793b25c04",
                        "source_sense_description": "zeitliche Definition im Sinne von Beginn",
                        "target_lang_word": "advent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "advent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19a91c53-a492-36f0-a611-b3faffdd7d51",
                                        "entry_id": "663203a0-589d-35ee-bfcf-ace960d9939b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Arrival; onset; a time when something first comes or appears; the time when it is approaching."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5258e6b-97a0-4ac2-928e-311ef226584e",
                                                "sense_id": "19a91c53-a492-36f0-a611-b3faffdd7d51",
                                                "text": "Death's dreadful advent"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca2fee9a-8b61-407c-b7c3-20f5a9dacd2f",
                                                "sense_id": "19a91c53-a492-36f0-a611-b3faffdd7d51",
                                                "text": "At the period just preceding the advent of Bartleby, I had two persons as copyists in my employment, and a promising lad as an office-boy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "442621e8-40b9-4b75-91a5-69e5fefad3aa",
                                                "sense_id": "19a91c53-a492-36f0-a611-b3faffdd7d51",
                                                "text": "The car in which I had taken Olivia to dinner and then out to the cemetery — a historic vehicle, even a monument of sorts, in the history of fellatio's advent onto the Winesburg campus in the second half of the twentieth century — went careening off to the side..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52542291-8ec1-4bd4-a3d3-79081e14b0cf",
                                                "sense_id": "19a91c53-a492-36f0-a611-b3faffdd7d51",
                                                "text": "Berlin's six-decade career began before the advent of radio and ended during the height of Beatlemania."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "advent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74c75126-efa5-3ce6-a49a-a4faa846f4b9",
                                        "entry_id": "4b46486e-47ea-30bd-a1a9-c07d94dadaaa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To arrive or begin, especially at the first coming or appearance of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df55cd4b-df93-4725-8ce7-b7c2863e129b",
                                                "sense_id": "74c75126-efa5-3ce6-a49a-a4faa846f4b9",
                                                "text": "1869 Grove Berry. Ritualism; Part II of An Enquiry. Pub: LONGMANS, GREEN et al.\nBut suppose we depart from the suggestion there made, and, leaving the idea of the status quo from which He advented to Earth, we rise with Solomon (Prov. viii), to some stasis which must be indefinite to us, are we not presumptuous if not even unpractical, Gnostical, and merely scholastic?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83b9558d-118f-400f-9706-1bdc7143f8b4",
                                                "sense_id": "74c75126-efa5-3ce6-a49a-a4faa846f4b9",
                                                "text": "The new Democratic war-horse from Calaveras has lately advented in the Legislature with a little bill to change the name of Tretherick to Starbottle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7d9ede9-3c03-4413-9ed3-324fcc07bf12",
                                                "sense_id": "74c75126-efa5-3ce6-a49a-a4faa846f4b9",
                                                "text": "1978 Mohammed Ahmad Qureshi. Marriage and Matrimonial Remedies: A Uniform Civil Code for India\nMaulana Abdul Kalam Azad in Tarjuman-ul-Quran says that in the seventh century when Islam was advented males had uncontrolled rights."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f669ce2-f3b6-4d77-b122-cf192e13c1e0",
                                                "sense_id": "74c75126-efa5-3ce6-a49a-a4faa846f4b9",
                                                "text": "2014 Adam Pryor. The god who lives.\nIn the flesh, self and world are always coming-to-be, adventing, in an intimate reciprocity to one another."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
